                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b] Story [/b]\n\nThe story of Icebound revolves around Dougal and Isaac, an alchemist and his familiar who made a terrible mistake, and search for a way to rectify it. Along the way they meet many characters and explore new lands. \n\n[b]Art: [/b]\n\nThe art is decent, there is a variety of art for each character, as well as CG's for important scenes.\n\n[b]Gameplay[/b]\n\nThis VN does feature some gameplay in the form of Alchemy puzzles. These involve placing colored squares in the right order to fill up a board, these can be quite challenging, and can be a fun break from reading.\n\n[b]Music[/b]\n\nThe music and sound design is well done, the music compliments the scenes nicely and flows seamlessly with the game.\n\n[b]Overall[/b]\n\nPlayers who enjoy fantasy or steampunk novels wil enjoy Icebound, it features a refreshing story with interesting plot points and mystery to keep you interested, and gameplay and puzzles will keep you coming back for more.",
